// Giving a list back. The compiler calls this (as id_list_free) for a local
// list it proved nothing else can reach; the header and the cell array go onto
// the free lists in mem/store/arena/more/pool.id and the elements are left to
// whoever else holds them, the same shallow free the hosted runtime does.
//
// A kernel has no stderr to trap to, so the hosted runtime's use-after-free
// guard has no equivalent here. The one thing this does check is a list freed
// twice, by a cap of -1 that no live list has: a second free is ignored rather
// than linking a block into a free list twice.

list_free(int[] xs) {
  word p = l2w(xs);
  if(p != 0 && ld64(p + 8) > 0) {
    list_give(p);
  }
} return void;
